 FREE:,NAME,
C===========================================================
C free(p, size) - return SIZE words at P to the heap allocator.
C
C Calling convention for a two-argument ASSEMBLER routine:
C   ACC        = size
C   [SP-1]     = p
C   M13        = return link
C
C P/DS expects M9 to address a cell containing p and M14 to hold size.
C STI moves size to M14 and pops p, leaving SP at the cell that still contains
C p.  Point M9 there; P/DS reads mem[M9] before its first push reuses the cell.
C===========================================================
 P/DS:          ,SUBP,
                ,STI ,14     . M14 := size; pop p, leaving SP at its cell
            15  ,MTJ ,9      . M9 := &p
                ,UJ  ,P/DS   . tail call; P/DS returns through caller's M13
                ,END ,
